From: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:47:31 -0500
Subject: [ganesh] Handle negative determinants in StrokeIterator for hairline
 square caps

A negative determinant is perfectly valid, e.g. from a negative Y scale.
Without this fix, the outset to form a square cap on zero-length
lines would be length 1 in local space, but the negative Y scale could
scale this square arbitrarily large.

Using |det| could work, but would result in flipping the square
(not visually noticeable). Instead I opted to just always apply the
inverse determinant and then check for finiteness afterwards to
handle scenarios where the outset itself overflows when det was a
subnormal value.

Bug: 578685477
Change-Id: I843ac39e92dfd927de82bf0ca87e3a02c8e9ab26
Fixed: 578685477
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1420276
Commit-Queue: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas Smith <thomsmit@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Greg Daniel <egdaniel@google.com>

diff --git a/src/gpu/tessellate/StrokeIterator.h b/src/gpu/tessellate/StrokeIterator.h
index 70ad3974c84f147b378b789cdff6d231ec3fcbd0..4db397e0ad49926d879c3e5cc80a49a5541b7bed 100644
--- a/src/gpu/tessellate/StrokeIterator.h
+++ b/src/gpu/tessellate/StrokeIterator.h
@@ -245,19 +245,18 @@ private:
                         SkASSERT(!fViewMatrix->hasPerspective());
                         float a=fViewMatrix->getScaleX(), b=fViewMatrix->getSkewX(),
                               c=fViewMatrix->getSkewY(),  d=fViewMatrix->getScaleY();
-                        float det = a*d - b*c;
-                        if (det > 0) {
-                            // outset = inverse(|a b|) * |.5|
-                            //                  |c d|    | 0|
-                            //
-                            //     == 1/det * | d -b| * |.5|
-                            //                |-c  a|   | 0|
-                            //
-                            //     == | d| * .5/det
-                            //        |-c|
-                            outset = SkVector{d, -c} * (.5f / det);
-                        } else {
-                            outset = {1, 0};
+                        // outset = inverse(|a b|) * |.5|
+                        //                  |c d|    | 0|
+                        //
+                        //     == 1/det * | d -b| * |.5|
+                        //                |-c  a|   | 0|
+                        //
+                        //     == | d| * .5/det
+                        //        |-c|
+                        outset = SkVector{d, -c} * sk_ieee_float_divide(0.5f, a*d - b*c);
+                        if (!SkIsFinite(outset.fX, outset.fY)) {
+                            // Don't outset any geometry if the matrix is not invertible.
+                            outset = {0, 0};
                         }
                     }
                     fEndingCapPts = {*fLastDegenerateStrokePt - outset,
